{
 "id": "card_limit_change",
 "request": "Branch staff ask for a card's daily limit to change by calling a webhook with card_id, requested_limit and reason. Look up the card's current daily limit in core banking. If the card isn't there, reply 404 with {status: 'not_found'} and do nothing else. A decrease, or the same limit, is applied straight away. An increase needs a credit officer: send the task to CREDIT_OFFICER_EMAIL, show them the card, the current and requested limit and the reason, let them enter the limit they approve as approved_limit (it can be lower than asked), and make them give a reason when they reject. If the credit officer hasn't decided within 4 hours, escalate the same task to the head of credit (HEAD_OF_CREDIT_EMAIL), due within 1 day; if that runs out too, it is rejected. When a change goes ahead, set the new limit through the cards API (for an increase, the limit the approver entered), then record it in ops_db in one transaction: a limit_changes row (card, old limit, new limit, reason) and an audit_log row (entity 'card', the card id, action 'limit_change'). Reply 200 with {status: 'applied', limit: <new limit>} or {status: 'rejected', reason: <the approver's reason, empty if nobody decided>}.",
 "apis": [
  "cards.yaml"
 ],
 "tables": {},
 "expect": {
  "trigger": "Webhook",
  "must_have_types": [
   "Postgres",
   "Approval",
   "Respond"
  ],
  "must_call": [
   "cards.setLimit"
  ],
  "max_nodes": 24,
  "min_types": {
   "Approval": 2
  }
 },
